## Harness engineering

This repo uses the Harness Adoption Starter to assess and grow its
engineering harness. The skills are tool-neutral runbooks under
`harness-adoption/skills/`.

When asked to **assess / score / find gaps**, read and execute
`harness-adoption/skills/assess.md` (read-only).

When asked to **adopt / set up a control / close the top gap**, read and
execute `harness-adoption/skills/adopt.md` (writes one control at a time,
with approval).

When asked to **audit** the harness, read and execute
`harness-adoption/skills/audit.md`.

The control library the skills reason from is `harness-adoption/patterns/`;
shared theory and templates (harness model, readiness rubric, scorecard,
spec/ADR templates) are under `harness-adoption/reference/`.

Conventions for this repo's harness:
- The canonical guide file is **this `AGENTS.md`**. Keep it concrete and
  current; every path it references must exist.
- There is one `check` command that runs format + lint + types; the gate
  runs exactly that. A check that only warns is not a gate.
- Fast checks run pre-commit/pre-push; expensive and LLM-based checks run
  in CI. Never put an LLM gate on the fast path.
